message: >-
  If you use this rule, its proof, or this implementation, please cite it using
  the metadata below.
title: "Grand Unified Divisibility Rule (Lemi's Formula)"
abstract: >-
  A single algorithm that generates the divisibility rule of every divisor,
  using no prime factorization and no division. A number is divisible by d
  exactly when the weighted sum of its digits is divisible by d, where the
  weight of the ones digit is 1 and every subsequent weight is the previous one
  multiplied by 10 and then reduced below d by repeated subtraction; the final
  total is the exact remainder. The classical rules for 2, 3, 4, 7, 8, 9 and 11
  are rows of the resulting table. Generalizes an equation discovered by the
  author in 1997, whose hidden validity criterion -- gcd((y*a2)+1, d) = 1 -- is
  identified here and shown to be the reason the original formulation required
  prime factorization.
type: software
